{#
    Light ↔ dark, saved to the account.

    A form, so it works with no script: it posts the opposite of the account's
    setting and the server sends the reader back to the page they were on.
    With htmx the same post swaps the root's `data-theme` in place — see the
    `renovo:theme` handler in app.js — and nothing reloads.

    An account on "system" is the one case the server cannot settle, because
    only the browser knows what the system is showing. The form says "dark"
    for it, and the script corrects that to the opposite of whatever is
    actually on screen before it is sent. Choosing "system" again is on the
    profile page, which is where all three states are offered.

    Both icons are in the markup and the stylesheet shows the one that
    matches what the page is wearing, including under "system", so the icon is
    right on first paint with no script.

    `user`       the signed-in User
    `return_to`  the path to come back to
#}
{% set theme = user.themePreference().value %}
{% set next = theme == 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark' %}
{% set label = next == 'dark' ? t('shell.theme_to_dark') : t('shell.theme_to_light') %}
<form class="theme-toggle" method="post" action="/profile/theme"
      hx-post="/profile/theme" hx-swap="none"
      data-label-light="{{ t('shell.theme_to_light') }}"
      data-label-dark="{{ t('shell.theme_to_dark') }}">
    {{ csrf_field() }}
    <input type="hidden" name="theme" value="{{ next }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="return" value="{{ return_to }}">
    <button type="submit" class="icon-button" title="{{ label }}">
        {{ icon('dark', 'icon-button-icon theme-toggle-dark') }}
        {{ icon('light', 'icon-button-icon theme-toggle-light') }}
        <span class="visually-hidden" data-theme-toggle-label>{{ label }}</span>
    </button>
</form>
